<title>USA: AMR's SABRE Group 1996 oper loss widens.</title>
<headline>AMR's SABRE Group 1996 oper loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.17		    $0.25</p>
<p> Net			     23			 32</p>
<p> Revs			   376			368</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.43		    $1.73</p>
<p> Net			    187			226</p>
<p> Revs			 1,622		    1,529</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: On a pro forma basis, 1996 Q4 net was $24 million, or $0.18 a share, an increase of 80.5 percent over 1995's pro forma results.</p>
<p>Pro forma amounts reflect the effect of new contracts with American Airlines, which were effective Jan 1, 1996, and the effect of certain other transactions resulting from the legal reorganization of the company.</p>
<p>For the year ended Dec 31, pro form net was $188 million, or $1.44 a share, an increase of 19.8 percent over 1995 pro forma.</p>
</text>
